# 105 - Project-Local Database

**Phase:** 1 (Foundation)
**Effect:** Database lives within project, custom world data tracked in git
**Status:** Completed (2026-01-29)

---

## The Effect

The database is project-local at `mysql/`. Custom world modifications (loot tables, NPC changes, balance tweaks) are tracked in git alongside code.

This enables:
- `git diff` shows world data changes
- Revert broken balance changes
- Collaborate on world design
- Clone repo → databases included
- No conflicts with system MySQL or other projects

---

## What This Solved

### Before

MySQL at `/home/ritz/programs/mysql-server/` was:
- Shared across multiple projects
- Not version controlled
- Custom changes lost on reinstall
- Risk of breaking other projects' databases

When tweaking loot drop rates or NPC spawn locations, changes were invisible to git. No history, no revert, no collaboration.

### After

MySQL at `mysql/` within project:
- Binaries at `mysql/installed-files/` (git-ignored, can rebuild)
- Databases at `mysql/databases/` (tracked in git)
- Config at `mysql/conf/my.cnf` (tracked)
- Port 3307 (coexists with system MySQL)

Custom world changes now show in `git diff`:
```
modified:   mysql/databases/acore_world/creature.ibd
modified:   mysql/databases/acore_world/creature_loot_template.ibd
```

