## Lessons Learned

### Binary Files in Git

Tracking `.ibd` files (InnoDB tablespace) in git is unconventional. Most projects use SQL dumps. We chose direct file tracking because:

**Pro:** Simplicity - no export/import steps
**Con:** Large diffs, merge conflicts

If this becomes painful, migrate to:
```
sql/custom/db_world/creature_loot.sql
sql/custom/db_world/gameobject_loot.sql
```

And load these on server start.

### Port Isolation

Using port 3307 instead of 3306 allows:
- System MySQL coexists
- Multiple wow-chat projects (each with own port)
- No "MySQL is already running" conflicts

This pattern works for development. Production might use Docker containers or separate VMs.

### MySQL Version Jumps

MySQL 9.x breaking `innodb_log_file_size` was discovered through error logs. When upgrading major versions, read changelogs for deprecated options.

Lesson: Don't blindly upgrade databases. Test in isolation first.

